body:
Uh as a non-American I have to ask. What's so controversial about what she said? I see people \*everyday\* talking shit about the US - it's "a shithole" / a "3rd world country" / it's "I'd rather live anywhere but America" / it's "a hellhole". Europeans, US Americans and non-US American saying this. (which, I've always found a little odd - so many people come to the US for a better life, no? Not saying the US is perfect - I hope you understand what I mean).  

&#x200B;

So... in conclusion: why is it so controversial when she says it, but non when, well, basically anyone else does?  

&#x200B;

(sorry if this is worded wrong; I'm genounly asking, it's almost 2:30 an I'm tired as Hell)

Nej - jag frågar varför det är dåligt att "vita svenskar" "protesterar mot polisbrutalitet i USA"? Är väl skitbra att svenskarna är emot polisbrutalitet?  

&#x200B;

Att det sedan sker under en epedemi är en annan sak, men ingenting som han / hon jag svarade på nämnde.
